src += "DESCRIPTION = (\n"
src += "'A no-bias ReLU RNN is homogeneous of degree one, so only the direction of x can matter for the decision. '\n"
src += "'Stage 1: h1 = max(x1,0)*A + max(-x1,0)*B with A=relu(Wx), B=relu(-Wx) -- the first state is just the positive and the '\n"
src += "'negative part of input 1 on two fixed rays, a two-dimensional variable (p1,n1). '\n"
src += "'Stage 2: h2 = relu(x2*Wx + p1*(A@Wh) + n1*(B@Wh)) lies in the relu of the span of the four vectors '\n"
src += "'[Wx,-Wx,A@Wh,B@Wh], which span only three dimensions, so seven spanning coordinates of h2 plus their lstsq '\n"
src += "'completion give the state exactly. Stage 3: same construction with ten spanning coordinates. '\n"
src += "'Steps 4-10 are carried as the full hexadecimal state: I could not find a smaller exact generating set there '\n"
src += "'(the reachable state fills the space; Wh has full rank, no sparsity, no rotational block structure), so the '\n"
src += "'wiring of those steps is stored once per distinct value, each weight rounded to a two-thousandth, which is 348 '\n"
